    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Prime ministers come and go in the U.K., but Larry, the “Chief Mouser” of 10 Downing Street, isn’t going anywhere. The grey-and-white "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "tabby",
            "zh": "虎斑猫"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " has lived there for over 15 years. He walks around the heart of government as if he were the one in charge."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Cats have been helping out in the English government since the 1500s. However, official records of these cats only go back to 1929. Back then, the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Treasury",
            "zh": "财政部"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " agreed to pay a small amount of money each day to care for a “skilled mouser.” Over time, this cat budget slowly grew."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Before Larry, Sybil served in the government office. She started her job in 2007 but left two years later. After that, there wasn’t an official mouser for a while. Rats were seen running around Downing Street. News reports even showed them during TV broadcasts. People began to wonder if a new cat was needed to solve "
          },
          {
            "t": "underline",
            "v": "the problem"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Soon after, Larry was brought in. The prime minister at the time, David Cameron, and his family chose him from an animal rescue centre."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Larry is not just responsible for catching rats. According to his official government page, his duties also include “greeting guests, checking the security system, and testing old furniture for sleeping quality”. As a top cat, he has grown very used to media attention. “The minute something happens on the street, especially an official visit, he’ll be out the front,” said a government worker. “He loves the red carpet.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Larry’s popularity with the public is clear. He has various social media accounts run by his fans. Larry also receives letters and toys from around the world. And last November, he appeared in the documentary, "
          },
          {
            "t": "em",
            "v": "David Baddiel: Cat Man"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". For his fans, this moment has been a long time coming."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
